.nh
.TH "PB-RSYNC" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-rsync - Run rsync with Paperboat machine resolution


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb rsync <standard rsync arguments...> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run rsync with Paperboat machine resolution

.PP
Run standard rsync arguments with Paperboat device-name resolution and authorized connectivity. File selection, deletion flags, and exit behavior remain rsync's responsibility; inspect its command line before synchronizing.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rsync


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
